From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Fri, 28 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: fix special summon counters, reflected damage and
 opponent_of reads at n > 2

The stock code reads or writes the opponent seat with opponent_of at several
sites. With more than 2 duelists that is seat 255 or the wrong seat. Every
change below is in an n_duelists > 2 branch. The n == 2 text is unchanged.

Special summon (SpSummon case 0 and case 2): each card is counted for its own
summon player. hint_timing and set_spsummon_counter run once per summon player,
the turn player first, then clockwise.
Reflect damage (Damage case 0 and case 1): the damage goes to the reason player
when that is a living duelist that is not on the holder's team. Otherwise
nobody takes it and the holder takes none. The normal damage messages and
lp_ref are used for the new target.
SelfDestroyUnique case 0: the choice list walks the living duelists clockwise
(own cards first, then the others, first with the unique place, then all). If
no card is valid the step ends, so the prompt cannot get an empty list.
SendTo case 6: a card without a controller no longer writes hint_timing and
check_decktop_visibility at seat 255.
Draw (deck_reversed confirm): one MSG_CONFIRM_CARDS for each living opponent.
TossDice: the count2 dice go to the first living opponent clockwise (one
opponent, so the result count stays count1 + count2).
is_player_can_discard_deck_as_cost: a redirect effect is checked against the
CANNOT_REMOVE state of its own handler player.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UrYy4jjEcbJHKdcVYasfdb
